@@host: England, eighteen-ninety. A folklorist named Joseph Jacobs gathers up the tales that English children already knew by heart, and prints them for the first time in one book.

@@host: This one was older than anyone could remember. It has a rhyme to start it, a wolf who will not give up, and a third little pig who is a great deal cleverer than he looks.

